# .gitleaksignore — per-FINDING suppressions for metadatastician/cadastra.
#
# One fingerprint per line:
#
#     <commit>:<path>:<rule-id>:<line>
#
# A fingerprint suppresses exactly one finding, in exactly one commit, at
# exactly one line. It is the narrowest suppression gitleaks offers, and it is
# deliberately not an allowlist: no rule is weakened, no path is blinded, the
# estate baseline is still staged and enforced, and the same pattern appearing
# in any other commit still fails the gate (a different commit produces a
# different fingerprint). Prefer this over `.gitleaks.toml` entries whenever the
# thing to suppress is a single historical fact that cannot be fixed forward.
#
# ── The one entry, and why it is a false positive ─────────────────────────────
#
# `.machine_readable/descriptiles/CLADE.a2ml` derives its UUIDv5 from the
# registry specification and, in an EARLIER revision of the file, showed the
# derivation with worked examples copied from the registry, one per line, in the
# form "<registry-name>  -> <UUIDv5>". The literal historical line is in commit
# 91e4666; it is not reproduced here because a scanner config that quotes its own
# fixtures is itself a finding (the working-tree pass scans this file too).
#
# `generic-api-key` reads that shape as a key/value assignment with high-entropy
# material and reports the UUID as a credential. It is not one: the "value" is a
# UUIDv5 that anyone can recompute from the rule printed directly above it
# (`uuid = UUIDv5(namespace = URL, name = "github.com/<owner>/<name>")`), and the
# current revision of the file has been reformatted to a table
# ("<UUIDv5> <- <registry-name>") precisely so the rule no longer matches.
#
# The finding survives only in history: commit 91e4666 (2026-07-16) still
# contains the arrow form, so the reusable's full-history gitleaks pass reports
# it on every run while the working-tree pass is clean. History cannot be
# rewritten to remove it — `main` is protected against non-fast-forward pushes —
# so the finding is suppressed by fingerprint and nothing else is touched.
#
# Verified against the pinned scanner's rule set: reproducing the reusable's
# full-history pass (gitleaks detect --source . --config .gitleaks-estate.toml)
# on a full clone reports exactly this one finding and exits 1; with this file in
# place it reports "no leaks found" and exits 0.
#
# Do NOT add an entry for a real secret. Rotate the credential and purge it from
# history; suppressing it here would leave it live and invisible.
91e466683bb899e35114211b997c08d98fa3cf96:.machine_readable/descriptiles/CLADE.a2ml:generic-api-key:13
